PATCH 623: preserve byte-only software-mixer normalization operands (board:0003).

Original 25f0/25fa, 2750/275a and 27b0/27ba execute MOV moffs8,AL at
2689/268b, 26b3/26b6 and 26df/26e2. Each operand belongs to a SHR/ADD
instruction; a word store also destroys its following opcode. Correct the
six shared symbol accessors to byte width so every decompiled entry into the
same original rollover blocks uses one storage contract.

The read-only paired original invocation at tick 11782 reaches a third-channel
rollover to its existing sample without a callback. The complete CPU trace
proves one rollover and 1024 stores. The regression compares full normalization
instruction bytes, the one-MiB isolated module state, every original mixed byte
in the selected DMA half and the untouched other half on native and WASM.
The parent corrupts adjacent code bytes on both targets. All six accessor widths
are backed by the original opcodes; the reaching fixture covers channel three.
Callback/register effects, other rollover variants, IRQ/device cadence and
elapsed mixer work remain open; no measured delay or callback substitute is added.
